@page "/components/notifications"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Notifications

<DocsHeader Title="Notification center" Eyebrow="Boards">
    <Lead>A bell that keeps notifications for later, so a toast that closed is not lost.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<DocExample Type="typeof(Bell)">
    <p>
        <code>StilNotificationCenter</code> shows a bell with the number of unread notifications. It opens a panel with
        them, newest first: choosing one marks it read and opens its page (<code>Href</code>), the cross removes it, and
        the panel can mark all as read or clear them. New ones are announced to screen readers.
    </p>
    <p>
        The notifications live in <code>IStilNotificationService</code>, one list per user session. A toast shown with
        <code>keep: true</code> is also kept there (<code>IStilToastService.Show(…, keep: true)</code>), and
        <code>AddStil(o =&gt; o.KeepToasts = true)</code> keeps every toast. Add your own with
        <code>Notifications.Add(message, title, variant, href)</code>. The newest 50 are kept
        (<code>MaxNotifications</code>). Put the bell in the navbar of an interactive layout.
    </p>
</DocExample>

